  "topic_en": "Ramanujan gives three rational generating functions with common denominator $1-82x-82x^2+x^3$ whose coefficients (in expansions in ascending and descending powers of x) yield infinitely many near-misses $a^3+b^3=c^3\\pm1$ to Fermat's equation, with numerical examples.",
  "transcription": "If\n\n(i) $\\frac{1+53x+9x^2}{1-82x-82x^2+x^3} = a_0+a_1x+a_2x^2+a_3x^3+\\cdots$\n$\\quad$ or $\\frac{\\alpha_0}{x}+\\frac{\\alpha_1}{x^2}+\\frac{\\alpha_2}{x^3}+\\cdots$\n\n(ii) $\\frac{2-26x-12x^2}{1-82x-82x^2+x^3} = b_0+b_1x+b_2x^2+b_3x^3+\\cdots$\n$\\quad$ or $\\frac{\\beta_0}{x}+\\frac{\\beta_1}{x^2}+\\frac{\\beta_2}{x^3}+\\cdots$\n\n(iii) $\\frac{2+8x-10x^2}{1-82x-82x^2+x^3} = c_0+c_1x+c_2x^2+c_3x^3+\\cdots$\n$\\quad$ or $\\frac{\\gamma_0}{x}+\\frac{\\gamma_1}{x^2}+\\frac{\\gamma_2}{x^3}+\\cdots$\n\nthen\n$a_n^3+b_n^3=c_n^3+(-1)^n$\nand $\\alpha_n^3+\\beta_n^3=\\gamma_n^3+(-1)^n$\n\nExamples\n$135^3+138^3=172^3-1$\n$11161^3+11468^3=14258^3+1$\n$791^3+812^3=1010^3-1$\n$65601^3+67402^3=83802^3+1$\n\n$9^3+10^3=12^3+1$\n$6^3+8^3=9^3-1$",
